WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
Here's what Learn gives you.

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:06.412
Get M P computer status shows tamper
and real-time protection, true when on.

3
00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:11.468
Get M P preference shows network
protection, zero off, one block, two audit;

4
00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:13.743
the two Windows Server settings;

5
00:00:13.743 --> 00:00:17.787
and controlled folder access,
with its disk-only modes too.

6
00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:23.051
Get net firewall profile, from the active
store, shows the firewall as enforced.

7
00:00:23.051 --> 00:00:25.750
And the guide's query
counts the audit and block

8
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.450
events and tampering
attempts over seven days.

9
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:34.674
Learn adds three conditions: network
protection needs the antivirus in active mode,

10
00:00:34.674 --> 00:00:38.675
needs its own setting on
Windows Server 2019 and later,

11
00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:45.050
and needs datagram processing off on domain
controllers, DNS, file and SQL servers.
